ster and faster  a huge evacuation order is in place more  than 6 000 people have left their homes  already as the fire traveled at  frightening speed  spitting out embers that fell as far as  two miles away  this wildfire comes as a record heat  wave is sweeping the united states with  heat warnings and emergencies declared  in several states  everything that's burning in the fire is  extremely dry we know that  california has been dry the last few  years and has gotten drier we just asked  that the public be patient if their  neighborhood or their community has been  affected by the fire it will take a  little while to notify them if they have  if their residents have been affected  climate change is driving the ferocity  of these fires the intense heat and  worst drought in decades spanning the  flames  but so far america has found no  political consensus on a way forward  that will do anything to prevent more of  this in the future  sally lockwood sky news washington  and before we go is there anything you  want to know about climate change what  confuses you or mystifies you we'll scan  the qr code on your screen right now to  submit your questions to us and we'll do  our best to answer them or you can go to  any of the sky news social media  accounts where you can add your  questions in the comments so get in  touch with us well that's all for now  for today we'll see you soon thanks for  watching  [Music]  you
 

